{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Files that define the shape of data crossing the API boundary, shown to the",
    "fix agent as read-only context. PR #130 misdiagnosed a crash because it could",
    "not see the type that declared the field non-null, nor the formatter that",
    "threw on it -- both ranked just under the 8-file cap. Ranking cannot fix that,",
    "so the repo declares them.",
    "",
    "Only features with a real finding behind them belong here. An earlier draft",
    "declared five more on speculation; every anchor in them was a stale-warning",
    "waiting to fire and none was ever exercised. Add one when a finding demands it.",
    "",
    "Rules: an anchor must match exactly one line (ambiguous or missing = the whole",
    "file is shown and the run reports it). 'editable: true' means the fix may land",
    "there; everything else is read-only. Terms-only features need distinctive",
    "phrases -- 'fleet' and 'vessel' match every finding in this app.",
    "",
    "Check with: python3 scripts/validate-qa-contracts.py"
  ],
  "features": [
